(BUF-53: the "Per-iteration use" worked example (LANGUAGE.md:3660-3672)
 — declaring a buffer inside a loop body and `Free`ing it at the end of
 each iteration — compiles and runs without crashing. The manual's own
 fragment omits the `total_lines`/`source` declarations (a `vox
 fragment`, not a complete program, same convention as other fragments
 in this manual); supplied here so it compiles. "Keeps memory flat" is
 an implementation-detail consequence, not observable from inside Vox —
 see the ledger row's `assertable?` note. `Read line from source into
 line` past EOF (the fixture is one line long) reads empty and does not
 error, so the loop runs to completion without an `On error` guard.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox BUF-53.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   This is a longer line of text than the buffer.

   loop finished
)
open a file for reading called source at "docs/ledger/probes/buffers/fixtures/long.txt".
a number called total_lines is 2.
a number called n is 0.
While n is less than total_lines,
    a buffer called line is 4096 bytes in size,
    Read line from source into line,
    print line as text,
    Free line,
    increment n.
Close source.
print "loop finished".
